    not_duplicate_of: []  # d3fc
    pr_ref:  # d3fc
    description: "Surfaced 2026-06-29 while attempting the WI-zipoj at-scale validation. 'hypergumbo run --path <flink>' (flink = ~14.6k Java source files, deep package hierarchies) timed out at BOTH a 30-minute and a 60-minute bound (rc=124). Both runs reached the SAME late stage — past the dependency-linker (UserWarning at cli.py:8434, 193430 Import edges) — and were killed during/after, i.e. in the finalization/sketch_precomputed phase. run_behavior_map's include_sketch_precomputed (cli.py:~8696) pre-extracts config_info, vocabulary, readme_description, AND additional_file_centrality_scores; the last involves a per-file EMBEDDING pass that is the suspected hot spot at 14.6k files. Because run never completed, no cache was written, so a subsequent 'sketch' auto-discovered no cache and re-ran analysis from scratch (also timed out). NEEDS ROOT-CAUSE: is the embedding/precompute pass O(files) but just expensive (~tens of min on 14.6k files) or super-linear? Profile run_behavior_map on flink (or kubernetes/Go for a faster-analyzing large repo). Distinct from WI-zipoj (sketch RENDERING at scale, now addressed by PR #321's comparison-sketch cache-read) and from INV-papuj (read-path cache reuse) — this is the ANALYSIS/precompute phase throughput at >1M LOC. Repro: 'hypergumbo run --path /home/jgstern_agent/ALL_REPOS/whole_bunch_of_repos/flink' under 'timeout 3600'."  # d3fc
    fields: {}  # d3fc
